# Fixed defect 132's class, 2026-09-29, a foreign word at the head of a line
# below an open one (lane 133's finding). Symptom: `constant A:` over
# `const B: i64`, `record P` whose field `x:` stands over `struct Q`, and
# `use` over `import geom` cost `continuation_outside_brackets` beside the
# lexer's `reserved_word`, and once `check --apply` had written `constant`,
# `record` or `use` the same open line cost `expected_type` or
# `expected_module_name`: one mistake under two codes, told in two turns.
# Cause: the lexer asked the next line's first word whether it starts a
# statement afresh, and a word it refuses is no keyword, so the line was
# joined. It now asks what the word's certain swap writes, as the parser reads
# it (`next_line.opening_keyword`, `foreign_at`), and the open line is ended
# there and told what it lacks in the parser's words. A hint or guidance
# names no word and is asked nothing.

use  #~ expected_module_name
import geom  #~ reserved_word

#~v expected_type
constant A:
const B: i64  #~ reserved_word missing_body
    5

record P
    #~v expected_type
    x:
struct Q  #~ reserved_word
    y: i64

function main()
    a = 1

    if a > 0
        #~v expected_expression
        x = a +
    elif a < 0  #~ reserved_word
        print(2)
